<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="018" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>NFR-11: fix useAnnounce's out-of-tree DOM lifecycle (React 19 unmount collision)</title>
    <phase>0 De-risk and baseline</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies a production `.ts` hook that IS the NFR-11 accessibility mechanism, and touches component lifecycle. Tags include `frontend` + `accessibility`.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>A well-understood React lifecycle defect with a named fix shape. Escalate if the correct fix turns out to require restructuring how the pane mounts.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches `shared/taskpane/hooks/` and will move the jest suite's pass/fail counts, which any concurrent test-touching task would then misattribute.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>017</deps>
    <tags>frontend, office-addins, accessibility, react, testing, tech-debt</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Fix `useAnnounce` so its ARIA live regions are owned by React rather than appended directly to `document.body`. This is a production defect in the NFR-11 accessibility mechanism, not a test problem.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer. React 19 lifecycle and ARIA live regions. Follow ADR-038 — do not adjust tests to fit a broken implementation.</role>

  <goal>`useAnnounce` no longer manipulates `document.body` outside React's tracked tree; announcements still reach assistive technology; and `useAnnounce.test.ts` passes on its own merits rather than by being rewritten to accommodate the defect.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Found by task 017 (2026-09-09) while proving that the `@testing-library/react` 14 → 16 bump did NOT fix the suite. 009 had hypothesized an RTL/React peer mismatch; 017 disproved it — the RTL bump changed nothing, and `useAnnounce.test.ts` still fails 16/16 with the identical `NotFoundError: The node to be removed is not a child of this node.`

      The real cause is production code. `shared/taskpane/hooks/useAnnounce.ts` calls `document.body.appendChild` at lines 76 and 96 and `document.body.removeChild` at lines 102 and 106, creating polite and assertive live regions OUTSIDE React's tracked tree. React 19's unmount bookkeeping collides with that: the node it expects to manage may already be gone, or belong to a parent React does not own. No testing-library version can fix it.

      This matters beyond the suite. `useAnnounce` IS the NFR-11 mechanism — "pane is keyboard-navigable with announced state changes". The 16 failing tests are detecting a real lifecycle bug in a spec-required accessibility feature.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/017-testing-library-alignment.md</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useAnnounce.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/__tests__/useAnnounce.test.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="017" status="complete">Established that the RTL version is NOT the cause, so this task starts from a correct diagnosis rather than 009's disproved one.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Prefer a React-owned target — a `createPortal` into a container the component itself renders, or regions rendered directly in the tree — over guarding `removeChild`. A parent-check guard silences the symptom while leaving the nodes outside React's ownership; only fall back to that if a portal genuinely cannot work, and say why.</constraint>
    <constraint source="adr">ADR-038 — the failing tests are the SPEC here. Do NOT rewrite assertions to match a broken implementation, and do NOT delete or skip a test to reach green. If a test's expectation is genuinely wrong, say so explicitly with reasoning before changing it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Accessibility behavior MUST be preserved: polite and assertive regions must remain distinct, must carry their existing ARIA attributes, and must still be announced. A fix that makes tests pass but stops announcing is a regression in the NFR-11 feature this task exists to protect.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT regress the production typecheck count. It is 0 as of 2026-09-09 (tasks 006/007/008); verify with `npm run typecheck` that it is still 0 when you finish.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope is `useAnnounce` and its test. The other 11 failing suites are separate mock/assertion defects and are NOT this task's job — report their count, do not fix them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Builds: `npm run build` IS the production build; it aborts at `webpack.config.js:24` without ADDIN_CLIENT_ID / TENANT_ID / BFF_API_CLIENT_ID / BFF_API_BASE_URL (non-secret values are in `.github/workflows/deploy-office-addins.yml`). Installs use `--legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`; never `npm ci`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The correct fix requires changing how the pane mounts, or moving live-region ownership into a shared provider that other components depend on. That is a structural change beyond a hook fix — STOP and report the scope.</trigger>
    <trigger>The tests turn out to encode an expectation that is itself wrong (e.g. asserting the node lands on `document.body` specifically). Report it and get the expectation confirmed before rewriting it — silently re-authoring assertions is what ADR-038 forbids.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`useAnnounce.ts` contains no direct `document.body.appendChild` or `document.body.removeChild` call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`useAnnounce.test.ts` passes 16/16 without assertions having been rewritten to accommodate the defect; any assertion that WAS changed is listed with its justification.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Polite and assertive live regions remain distinct and retain their ARIA attributes; a test pins that both still receive announcements.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` shows production errors still at 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The full suite's failing-suite count is reported before and after; suites other than `useAnnounce` are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No test deleted or newly skipped (ADR-038).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useAnnounce.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/__tests__/useAnnounce.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>
</task>
